  "text_md": "## aml = 0.02 aml = 0.02\n\n||am∗B||a3/2Φren|\n|---|---|---|---|\n||s||Bs|\n|q||ren Bq||\n|∗ B||2 Φ||\n||l|3/|Bl|\n\n*am a* 3*/*2Φren *am∗B a* APE APE\n\ntime slice time slice *aml* = 0*.*02 *aml* = 0*.*02\n\n||am∗B||a3/2Φren|\n|---|---|---|---|\n||s||Bs|\n|q||ren Bq||\n|∗ B||2 Φ||\n||l|3/|Bl|\n\n*am a* 3*/*2Φren *am∗B a* HYP HYP\n\n## time slice time slice\n\n∗ ren FIG. 1: Determination of m (left) and Φ (right) using the average of two time sources on Bq Bq the aml= 0.02 ensemble. The upper plots show the APE data, while the lower plots show the HYP-smeared data. For each panel, the shaded band corresponds to the plateau extracted from averaging the data over four consecutive time slices. Errors shown are statistical only.\n\nmatrix element divided by the Bq-meson mass:\n\nMBq= Mq/mBq. (66)\n\nFor the determination of MBq, we use different spatial sources for the two choices of link 3 smearing: in the case of APE-smeared links we use box sources of size 8, while for HYP smearing we use wall sources. The local-wall two-point functions are already defined in\n",
